WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.730
I hate that I was correct.

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:04.350
I really do.

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:09.440
But months ago, I told you other countries
are getting corona virus under control.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:10.810
We are not.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:14.410
It is looking more and more like at some point.

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:16.219
Travel is going to open back up.

00:00:16.219 --> 00:00:18.019
Asia, Europe, Europe.

00:00:18.019 --> 00:00:20.400
Two to two to wherever you go.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.400
It doesn't matter.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:26.509
Europe, Australia and the United States is
likely to be banned from entering a lot of

00:00:26.509 --> 00:00:27.539
these countries.

00:00:27.539 --> 00:00:28.539
Why?

00:00:28.539 --> 00:00:29.579
Because they've got it under control.

00:00:29.579 --> 00:00:30.579
We don't.

00:00:30.579 --> 00:00:32.789
And they don't want us bringing the disease
there.

00:00:32.789 --> 00:00:35.780
And unfortunately, that is exactly what is
happening.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:43.600
Europe reportedly plans, according to a report
in The New York Times, to ban American travelers

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:48.910
indefinitely because we are failing hard on
corona virus.

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:53.870
Now, when I say that we're failing, we haven't
all failed that.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:55.200
That's the reality.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.890
Some of the best places in the world to be
right now, places that have seen the most

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:04.000
rapid decrease in cases are in the United
States.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.250
I am fortunate to live in one of those places,
Massachusetts.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:13.440
But on the other side of the coin, many of
the worst places to be in the world are in

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:14.560
the United States.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:21.720
And if you are Switzerland or you are Spain
or France, you can't, practically speaking,

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.820
say people from Massachusetts can fly here.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:26.580
But people from Arizona can't.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:31.010
And the United States is going to be judged
by our worst performing states.

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:35.470
And unfortunately, the worst performing states
right now are some of the worst places in

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:36.830
the world to be.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:41.650
So what's going on is that on July 1st, Europe
is going to reopen its borders to international

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:47.660
travelers and they've put together a list
of countries that are not going to be allowed

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:48.660
to come in.

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:51.240
People from countries that are not going to
be allowed to come in.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:52.950
The list is still being finalized.

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:55.880
The United States is reportedly on the list.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:58.030
China is believed to be on the list.

00:01:58.030 --> 00:01:59.670
Uganda, Cuba, Vietnam.

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:04.630
It looks like Brazil and Russia, which are
disastrous hot spots.

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:07.280
They are believed to be on the list now.

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:10.320
On a personal level, this bothers me.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:12.050
But that's not what this is really about.

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:17.090
I mean, I was hoping I was planning to maybe
be able to go to Europe at the end of summer

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:20.140
if things were better there and things were
better here.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:22.700
But they're terrible here at the national
level.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:24.840
And so I'm not going to be allowed to go,
OK?

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:26.340
But, you know, sad for me.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:31.240
But there's a much bigger picture here because
this is a huge blow to the prestige and respect

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:33.750
of the United States around the world.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.870
We've already been a laughing stock since
Donald Trump was elected.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:39.150
It's gotten worse and worse and worse.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:43.840
And this is really an indictment of the job
that Donald Trump has done or maybe better

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.510
said, not done on the issue of Corona virus.

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:51.460
Trump is so unstable, we know how he's going
to react to this.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:55.950
And it's really tragic how terribly some parts
of our of our country are doing.

00:02:55.950 --> 00:03:02.319
For example, if you look at Spain, you see
that their cases have just fallen off a cliff.

00:03:02.319 --> 00:03:05.210
Such small numbers in Spain lately.

00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:10.319
You look at Switzerland, Switzerland has absolutely
crushed the curve.

00:03:10.319 --> 00:03:11.319
Looks amazingly good.

00:03:11.319 --> 00:03:13.020
I could go on giving you more and more examples.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:18.750
New Zealand, you know, many places in Europe
and around the world, here in the United States,

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.880
there are places that are looking very good.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:21.880
One of the.

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:23.680
Places that have seen the fastest decline
in cases.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:28.819
I'm proud to say, I'm happy to say is right
here in the Commonwealth of Massachusetts,

00:03:28.819 --> 00:03:31.730
where we are doing very well.

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:36.110
And, you know, we could say, hey, listen,
we have an airport, we have all sorts of flights

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:37.580
to Europe.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:44.670
But sadly, because anybody can just come to
Massachusetts from Florida or Arizona or Texas,

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:46.810
we're not going to be allowed into Europe.

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:50.510
And indeed, when you look at the numbers in
some of these other states, you look at Texas.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:52.319
Texas set a new record.

00:03:52.319 --> 00:03:58.230
Each of the last two days, Texas had more
than 5000 Corona virus cases two days in a

00:03:58.230 --> 00:03:59.230
row.

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:05.349
The last couple of days in Florida, around
30, 500 cases per day.

00:04:05.349 --> 00:04:08.720
In fact, they've been there for close to a
week.

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:11.930
Yesterday's Trump rally location, which we
will discuss later.

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:17.879
Arizona hitting their single day record yesterday,
same day as a Trump rally doesn't really bode

00:04:17.879 --> 00:04:19.809
well for 10 days from now.

00:04:19.809 --> 00:04:24.880
But more than thirty five hundred new cases
in Arizona yesterday for the first time.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:28.210
So we have to realize that we are the bad
eggs here.

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:32.809
We are that country that around the world,
along with Brazil and Russia and India.

00:04:32.809 --> 00:04:35.669
I mean, we're not unique in this way, but
we are one of the worst.

00:04:35.669 --> 00:04:40.430
We are one of those bad eggs that around the
world they say, hey, we're doing well.

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:41.759
Many countries are doing well.

00:04:41.759 --> 00:04:44.460
Let's start to restart economies and let people
in.

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:46.960
But we've got to keep the bad actors out.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:49.419
We are one of the bad actors right now.

00:04:49.419 --> 00:04:51.479
Now, this should not come as a shock.

00:04:51.479 --> 00:04:55.509
Our president admitted on Saturday that he
wanted testing slowed down.

00:04:55.509 --> 00:04:56.719
He confirmed it yesterday.

00:04:56.719 --> 00:04:58.620
I'll have video for you later.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:05.740
So when you hear the president wanted less
testing, it shouldn't come as a huge surprise

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:08.430
that we're not doing so well now.

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:13.620
I hesitate to even open up this can of worms
because it's being considered.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.409
I'm going to mention it.

00:05:15.409 --> 00:05:20.660
There is the possibility that some of the
states that are doing better are going to

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:25.740
look at banning travel from other American
states.

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:29.430
This is very complicated legally because of
the law.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:38.159
Paul v. Virginia from, I believe, 1869, the
Supreme Court defined freedom of movement

00:05:38.159 --> 00:05:45.150
in the United States as a right of free ingress
to other states and egress from them.

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:47.070
And that seems very cut and dry.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:53.879
But there's many different layers and overlapping
precedent when it comes to what is there in

00:05:53.879 --> 00:05:58.449
terms of what states can do to say we're not
letting people in from Florida or we're not

00:05:58.449 --> 00:06:00.479
letting people in from Texas.

00:06:00.479 --> 00:06:06.069
There are discussions happening about northeastern
states saying we don't want people coming

00:06:06.069 --> 00:06:08.250
here from those other places.

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:09.449
Could be Massachusetts.

00:06:09.449 --> 00:06:11.240
New York is looking at it.

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:18.069
Is it possible that if certain states did
that they would be allowed to send people

00:06:18.069 --> 00:06:20.099
to Europe on planes?

00:06:20.099 --> 00:06:21.099
We don't know.

00:06:21.099 --> 00:06:25.349
And it really depends more on Europe than
it does on on us.

00:06:25.349 --> 00:06:27.749
The legal questions are complex.

00:06:27.749 --> 00:06:31.349
This is also going to cause absolute and total
chaos.

00:06:31.349 --> 00:06:34.619
And it is going to start to get very ugly
in the United States.

00:06:34.619 --> 00:06:39.909
If you start seeing and it's being considered
now certain states saying we are sort of going

00:06:39.909 --> 00:06:45.380
to isolate our state as if it were its own
country.

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:48.930
And I mean, listen, I'll maybe leave it there
for now.

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:52.840
If that happens, there will be many more conversations
to have.

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:54.020
Before we go to the break.

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:56.639
I want to say thank you.

00:06:56.639 --> 00:07:00.470
We had something very special happen yesterday
on the show yesterday.

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:02.710
You know, we've been doing the show for years
and years and years.

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:04.580
Yesterday, the same day, right.

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:05.580
June.

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:06.580
Twenty third.

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:10.639
We had our best day for the audio podcast
ever.

00:07:10.639 --> 00:07:13.020
You go back to the start of the audio podcast.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:21.069
We had more listens to the audio podcast yesterday
than ever in David Pakman show history.

00:07:21.069 --> 00:07:28.270
Also yesterday, on the same day, we had more
people watch our clips on Facebook than ever

00:07:28.270 --> 00:07:29.270
before.

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:34.169
So yesterday was the best day in the David
Pakman show's history, storied history, controversial

00:07:34.169 --> 00:07:41.699
history ever in terms of Facebook views and
podcast downloads.

00:07:41.699 --> 00:07:43.340
And I just have you guys to thank.

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:45.099
I so appreciate it.

